04d28). The scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart evidence protocol (cmd-cb8d0e2541224cea), and its transient unit did not leave observed residue after reboot. All other recorded commands were read-only validation or bounded restart polling. Post-execution evidence shows no failed services, new exposure, damaged package state, or unrelated temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d698455696704d28","cmd-cb8d0e2541224cea","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the scheduled restart, changed boot identity, and recovered its services and restored data. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
